 4. 🗳️ Map du jour: &#x27;26 election stickers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Images collected by Ballotpedia and Jim Sergent/Axios No city or state requires an "I Voted" sticker, but they've become an Election Day staple across America, Ballotpedia notes. 

 Some have classic red, white and blue designs, some feature state landmarks and some are even sketched by the voters or their kids for local contests. More about the stickers . 

 
 
