 5. 💰 Pocketbook blues 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : University of Michigan. Chart: Courtenay Brown/Axios One of the final snapshots of how Americans feel about the economy before voters head to the polls shows a nation still deeply frustrated by the cost of living, Axios' Courtenay Brown reports. 

 The University of Michigan's consumer sentiment index registered 48 in October — 10% below its level this time last year. The intrigue: Separate data released alongside the index showed that the share of Republicans citing high prices as a drag on their finances has surged roughly 50 percentage points since January, a much larger increase than among Democrats or independents.

