 8. 🎸 1 fun thing: 20 years of Tay 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Taylor Swift performs for "The Eras Tour" at Nissan Stadium in Nashville in May 2023. Photo: John Shearer/TAS23/Getty Images for TAS Rights Management Taylor Swift's self-titled debut album — featuring smash hits like " Teardrops on My Guitar ," " Our Song " and " Tim McGraw " — turns 20 today.

 Why it matters: For all the genres and eras Swift has explored since, that first collection of songs reveals just how much of the artist she'd become was there from the start, Axios Nashville's Adam Tamburin writes. Zoom in: As journalist Emily Yahr writes in her new book "Taylor Swift: The Debut Years," many executives were skeptical that Swift's point of view would resonate with their target audience of 30-something women listening to the radio during carpool runs. 

 But Swift insisted on writing for the kids in the back seat. 📝 By the numbers: Swift wrote or co-wrote more than 100 songs while preparing to release "Taylor Swift," Yahr says. The 11 tracks that made the cut leaned unapologetically into teenage experiences.

 The effervescent "Our Song," a classic Swiftian anthem that she wrote on her own for a freshman talent show, crackled with the giddy excitement of puppy love. She eventually released it as the third single off of her debut album. It was her first to hit No. 1 on the country charts.

